Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the FX Regime Lab project.

## What was implemented:

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Identified Next.js-specific installation instructions for the project

### 2. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version 2.0.0) using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

### 3. Configured SpeedInsights Component
Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout, placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Followed Next.js App Router best practices by placing it in the body of the root layout

## Implementation Details:

The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout following the official documentation:
- Placed after the main app content and Analytics component
- Uses the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- No additional configuration required - works out of the box

## Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Verification:
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Linter check passed for modified files (no new errors introduced)
- ✅ All changes staged with git
